 "input": "association apiary. members inspect hives weekly in season, inspection notes go on the hive record cards (queen seen, brood, disease signs). swarm calls from the public go to the swarm coordinator who sends a member and logs it. varroa treatment in autumn, timing from mite counts on the record cards, treatment recorded for the vet medicine log (legal requirement). honey harvest in August, extracted in the shared extraction room booked on the room calendar, jars labelled with the association label. honey sales money to the treasurer. beginners course each spring uses the apiary hives.",
